{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"constant term constant term","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md","fileName":"Constant Term.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Constant Term","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Algebraic Expressions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algebraic Expressions","Algebraic Term","Algebraic Simplification","Polynomial Long Division","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"constant term constant term","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md","fileName":"Constant Term.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Constant Term","heading":"Constant Term","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A constant term is an [[Algebraic Term]] whose value does not depend on a variable. In (3x^2-5x+7), the term (7) is constant.\n\nConstants behave as like terms with other constants, so they can be combined during [[Algebraic Simplification]]. Their role depends on the surrounding form. In a linear expression (ax+b), (b) shifts the value independently of (x); in a polynomial, the constant is the term of degree zero. Writing it explicitly can also preserve place structure during [[Polynomial Long Division]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Algebraic Expressions","Algebraic Term","Algebraic Simplification","Polynomial Long Division","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Constant Term.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"constant term c